course: dictionary
lesson: 1404
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word carcass usually means the dead body of an animal. «Tasmanian devils crunch whole carcasses, bones and fur included» tells you a carcass is a whole animal body, with its bones and fur still on it.
explain: Context clues help you choose the right meaning. In «Mum boiled the turkey carcass to make soup», the words boiled and soup show that carcass means the bones left after the meat has been eaten. Try the meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
explain: Carcass can also mean the frame or broken remains of something, such as an old car. Informal speech, like a joke, can use it for your body: «Get your carcass off the sofa!» Here it is a silly, jokey way to say your body.
fact: Carcass means the dead body of an animal, especially a large one.
fact: The carcass of a cooked chicken or turkey is the bones left after the meat is eaten.
fact: Carcasses is the plural. In UK spelling you may also see carcase.
fact: Scavengers such as vultures, hyenas and crows feed on carcasses.
fact: A carcass can also be the frame or broken remains of something, like an old car or building.
exercise: «Tasmanian devils crunch whole carcasses, bones and fur included.» What does carcass mean here? | *The dead body of an animal | A tin can for food | A live animal running free | A sharp bone from a fish
exercise: Mum says, «We will boil the turkey carcass for soup.» What is the carcass in this sentence? | *The bones left after the meat has been eaten | A whole live turkey on the farm | The turkey's soft feathers | A pan of hot soup
exercise: «The carcass of the old car rusted in the field.» What does carcass mean here? | A field full of long grass | A brand new engine | A dead cow lying in the grass | *The broken frame of something old
test: «Get your carcass off the sofa!» What does carcass mean in this jokey line? | *Your body | The bones of a chicken | A broken car | A dead animal
test: «Vultures feed on carcasses, and their strong stomach acid kills most germs.» What does carcasses mean? | *Dead animal bodies | Cooked meals | Live birds in flight | Frames of old cars
exam: Which sentence uses carcass to mean the bones left after a meal? | Get your carcass off the sofa | The carcass of the old bus stood by the road | A vulture landed on the carcass of a deer | *Mum boiled the turkey carcass to make soup
